}) | safe }}

<p class="prose">Last updated: <time datetime="{{ dateModified }}">{{ dateModified }}</time></p>

<section class="prose" aria-labelledby="content-error">
  <h2 id="content-error">A page says something wrong</h2>
  <p>
    Corrections are the most useful mail this site gets, and a correction
    with a source is the most useful kind.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Open a content-error issue</strong> on GitHub with the
      <a href="https://github.com/{{ site.repository }}/issues/new?template=content-error.yml">content-error form</a>.
      It asks for the page, the claim, and what you think is right. Issues
      are public, so do not put anything private in one.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Check the <a href="{{ '/errata/' | url }}">errata page</a></strong>
      first: it lists the corrections already made. How a correction is
      handled is described under
      <a href="{{ '/methodology/' | url }}#corrections">"When we're wrong"</a>
      in the methodology.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Or fix it yourself:</strong> every page footer has an "Edit
      this page on GitHub" link that opens the page source in the editor.
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="prose" aria-labelledby="security">
  <h2 id="security">A security problem</h2>
  <p>
    The site is static pages with a little browser JavaScript, and the only
    server-side piece is an optional database table that receives assistant
    votes and the Change Feed Playground's rows. Please report anything you
    find in that scope: a script injection, a leaked key or secret, a
    database permission that is too wide, or a vulnerable dependency.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Email</strong>
      <a href="mailto:{{ author.contactEmail }}">{{ author.contactEmail }}</a>.
      This is the maintainer's designated public address for security
      reports. Say which page or file, the steps to reproduce, and the impact.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Or use GitHub's private reporting</strong> from the repository's
      Security tab, as described in the
      <a href="https://github.com/{{ site.repository }}/blob/main/SECURITY.md">security policy</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>For tools:</strong> the standard
      <a href="{{ '/.well-known/security.txt' | url }}">security.txt</a>
      file carries the same contact. Under this project address it can be
      served only below the site's own path, not at the host root.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Please do not open a public issue for a vulnerability, and do not put
    real data, secrets or connection strings in a report. Reports are read
    by one person and a reply is not guaranteed within any particular time.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="prose" aria-labelledby="general">
  <h2 id="general">Anything else</h2>
  <p>
    For a question, a suggestion or a general message, write to
    <a href="mailto:{{ author.contactEmail }}">{{ author.contactEmail }}</a>
    or message {{ author.name }} on
    <a href="{{ author.advisoryUrl }}" rel="noopener">LinkedIn</a>. To ask
    what the assistant or the playground stored about you, or to ask for an
    entry to be deleted, read the
    <a href="{{ '/privacy/' | url }}#delete">privacy page</a> first.
  </p>
  <p>
    An email address is not a private channel from the web's point of view:
    this one is published on this page, so it can attract spam.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="prose" aria-labelledby="ai-assisted">
  <h2 id="ai-assisted">About how the content is written</h2>
  <p>
    Much of the text on this site is drafted with AI assistance. A page is
    described as reviewed by the maintainer only after he has confirmed that
    review. This is why correction reports matter: they are one way a wrong
    claim gets found.
  </p>
</section>
